sections.body:
Imagine defining a single API response contract that works for documents, agent outputs, users and Playwright reports without losing their specific types.

```typescript
type APIResponse<T> = {
    success: boolean;
    data: T;
};
```

In the next module, we will cover generic functions, generic interfaces, generic classes, constraints, `keyof`, `typeof`, indexed access types, `Partial`, `Required`, `Readonly`, `Pick`, `Omit`, `Record`, `ReturnType`, `Parameters`, `Awaited`, `Exclude`, `Extract`, `NonNullable`, conditional types, mapped types, `infer` and branded types.

We will also build a fully typed agent tool registry where TypeScript automatically associates each tool name with its specific input and output types.

